  "reference_answer": "Yeah, I'd say I do prefer big cities, though not everything about them appeals to me. The main draw is the sheer range of options — you can find pretty much any kind of food, job or evening class within a short train ride. I also like the fact that people are more anonymous, so you can just blend in and do your own thing. That said, the noise and the rent do wear you down after a while. So for now, big cities suit me, but I could see myself wanting somewhere quieter later on.",
