{
  "reference_answer": "Honestly, not really — I'd take a smaller place any day. The thing that gets me about big cities is how long everything takes. Seeing a friend who lives twenty minutes away can eat up half your evening once you've factored in the walk, the wait and the crowds. In a smaller town, that same catch-up is a ten-minute bike ride, so you actually do it instead of putting it off. I also like bumping into the same faces — the baker, the guy at the corner shop — it makes a place feel like yours. Big cities are exciting for a weekend, but I wouldn't want to live that pace every day.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：以“时间成本”为核心拒绝大城市，辅以熟人感与周末对比；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "any day",
      "meaning_zh": "任何时候都愿意；毫不犹豫地选择",
      "why_useful": "口语中表达强烈偏好的高频短语，比 I prefer 更自然、更有态度。",
      "example": "I'd choose a quiet beach over a crowded resort any day.",
      "usage_note": "常放在句尾，前面接 would + 动词。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the thing that gets me about",
      "meaning_zh": "让我最受不了/最在意的一点是",
